---
description: >-
  Spec #1368, #1432. Swimlane shape-data labels (a@{ label: … }) written five ways, one node
  each, across two lanes: plain, a quoted markdown string, a code span, tags, and a written
  backslash-n (single-quoted, so YAML keeps it). Markdown is read only in the markdown string;
  plain markers and the code span are drawn as written; the tags draw; the backslash-n breaks
  the line. Bare backticks are left out: YAML takes no unquoted backtick.
---
swimlane-beta LR
  subgraph L1 [written]
    A@{ label: "plain **bold** _ital_" }
    B@{ label: "`markdown string **bold** _ital_`" }
    C@{ label: "code span a `code` b" }
  end
  subgraph L2 [formatting]
    D@{ label: "tags <b>bold</b> <i>ital</i><br>next H<sub>2</sub>O" }
    E@{ label: 'written one\ntwo' }
  end
  A --> B --> C --> D --> E
